Paper 1: IoT-Based Smart Indoor Air Quality Monitoring Using CO₂ Sensors

	* Methodology: CO₂ sensor + IoT dashboard for real-time monitoring
	* Advantages: Real-time data; easy visualization
	* Limitations: Sensor drift; accuracy depends on calibration
	* Research gap: Long-term self-compensation to reduce drift impact

Paper 2: Calibration and Performance Evaluation of Low-Cost CO₂ Sensors

	* Methodology: Compare low-cost CO₂ sensors with reference instruments; use calibration approach
	* Advantages: Improves reliability; explains error sources
	* Limitations: Calibration can be time-consuming and manual
	* Research gap: Auto/less frequent calibration with adaptive correction

Paper 3: Machine Learning for CO₂ Concentration Prediction in Smart Buildings

	* Methodology: ML/time-series prediction using CO₂ + related signals (temperature/occupancy patterns)
	* Advantages: Predicts CO₂ trends; enables proactive control
	* Limitations: Needs sufficient training data; depends on building type
	* Research gap: Combine prediction with ventilation rules + handle occupancy uncertainty

Paper 4: Real-Time Anomaly Detection for Indoor Air Quality

	* Methodology: Detect unusual CO₂ spikes using streaming analytics/thresholding/ML
	* Advantages: Quick detection of harmful air quality episodes
	* Limitations: False alarms can occur due to sensor noise
	* Research gap: Robust anomaly detection considering noise and sensor drift

Paper 5: Energy-Efficient Ventilation Control Based on CO₂ Monitoring

	* Methodology: HVAC/ventilation control using CO₂ feedback to optimize energy
	* Advantages: Maintains air quality while saving energy
	* Limitations: Performance varies with HVAC system; measurement accuracy critical
	* Research gap: Scalable control logic + improved CO₂ measurement compensation

Common Overall Research Gaps

	* Low-cost CO₂ sensors have drift and bias
	* Need better calibration/compensation with minimal manual effort
	* Need integrated solution: sensing + prediction/anomaly detection + control/alerts

Conclusion for Your Project

	* Use IoT monitoring as base
	* Improve accuracy using calibration/compensation
	* Add real-time decision support using prediction/anomaly/alerts
